    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is headlined by **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.22) today, as both benefit from advantageous matchups against subpar opposing starters. **Jonathan Aranda** carries our highest efficiency score of the slate, bolstered by a significant 19% boost from facing Shane Bieber\u2019s 5.10 xERA. While we are currently waiting on an official lineup confirmation, his projected #2 spot provides him the volume required to anchor our offensive output. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a core start despite a slightly tougher individual matchup; his elite base projection and the added bonus of Bradley\u2019s slower delivery\u2014which creates a favorable environment for his stolen base potential\u2014keep his floor remarkably high. **Daulton Varsho** and **Geraldo Perdomo** also grade out as strong starts, with **Daulton Varsho** gaining meaningful value from a platoon advantage against Casey Legumina, while **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from an elevated role in the batting order against Michael McGreevy.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was benching **Gavin Sheets**, who fell just short of the 40.0 threshold with a score of 36.02. While he offered moderate power upside, the combination of a daunting matchup against Chris Sale (3.14 xERA) and an unfavorable platoon split pushed him into the \"Below Floor\" category, leading to his exclusion in favor of higher-efficiency options. Elsewhere, we remain cautious regarding the reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Masyn Winn**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Geraldo Perdomo**; their scores are highly sensitive to their confirmed spots in the batting order. We are also managing the absence of **Bryce Harper**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Lawrence Butler** due to team off-days, thinning our available depth. With **Masyn Winn** and **Geraldo Perdomo** both projected for stolen base opportunities against Pfaadt and McGreevy respectively, our primary objective remains maximizing category efficiency in the SB race while avoiding the pitfalls of low-probability starters like **Gavin Sheets**.",
